-------------------------------------------
BOSS 4.1 Release Note #  4   April 13, 1999
-------------------------------------------
_________________________________________________________________

(1) Switches NOBNDV and NOANGV have been added to BOSS and MCPRO,
to turn off (when set to 1) sampling of variable bonds and 
bond angles for the solute. The idea is to possibly use this
in equilibrations by local heating the solute and only varying
dihedral angles.

For mcpro16, the modified par file entry is

IRECNT, INDSOL, IZLONG, MAXOVL, NOXX, NOSS, NOBNDV, NOANGV
   0   1   0   0   0   0   0   0

For boss41, it is

 IRECNT, INDSOL, IZLONG, MAXOVL, NOXX, NOSS, NOBNDV, NOANGV:
  0  1  0  0  0  0  0  0

(The only difference is I4 vs I3)
_________________________________________________________________

(2) I have modified the assignment of dihedral ranges when done 
    automatically by the programs such that the ranges are
    +/- 15 degrees about bonds not in rings
    +/-  5 degrees about bonds in rings (should increase acceptance rate)
    +/-  2 degrees for improper dihedrals
    +/-  5 degrees about bonds with V2 > 3
    +/-  2 degrees about bonds with V2 > 4 (aromatics, alkenes,...)


